# Components

- Use functional client/server components as appropriate. Keep shadcn/ui
  primitives in `components/ui/`; app features live in `src/components/`.
- Target three-panel layout: phase stepper, chat, editable Project Brain.
- Project Brain shows structured Postgres state. Edits are user-owned;
  AI research-progress changes appear as proposed patches to accept or
  reject. Only profile fields may be filled in directly by the coach, and
  the UI says so with a chat notice.
- The AI teaches and critiques in chat (Markdown via `src/components/markdown.tsx`).
  Do not add paper-drafting, experiment, or ghostwriting UI. Scope is
  Phase 1 (Orient) and Phase 2 (Find your question).

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — apply model output directly
setProject(await chatResponse.state);

// ✅ GOOD — queue a patch for the user
setProposedPatch(validatedPatch);
```

- Do not put API keys (Groq, Gemini, Supabase service role) or model calls
  in client components. Call `/api/*` routes instead.
- Reuse existing dialogs, cards, buttons, and inputs rather than new kits.
